⍝ ZZ67_Regression.tc
⍝ ══════════════════

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ bug-apl@gnu.org, "Bugs found in r2047" (Blake McBride, 2026-07-24),
      ⍝ findings H17d/H17e: regression coverage for the ⌹/gelsy()/larfg()
      ⍝ overflow findings below. See SVN log for details.

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ⍝ H17e: larfg()'s BETA_r = sqrt(square(ALPHA) + norm2_X) squared
      ⍝ ALPHA directly, unscaled -- for ALPHA ≳ 1.34E154 that alone
      ⍝ overflows to +Inf, and tau = (BETA_r-ALPHA_r)/BETA_r then becomes
      ⍝ Inf/Inf = NaN. MM below is genuinely singular (both rows
      ⍝ proportional) and must fail with DOMAIN ERROR; with the bug it
      ⍝ silently returned -nan- -nan- / 0 1 instead.
      ⍝
      MM←2 2⍴1E160 1 1E160 1
      ⌹MM
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹MM
      ^
      )SIC

      ⍝ H17e, second reproducer: same root cause, different symptom --
      ⍝ with the bug this silently dropped the ¯1 element instead of
      ⍝ erroring or computing a correct (or correctly-refused) result.
      ⍝
      MM←2 2⍴1E200 0 1E200 1
      ⌹MM
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹MM
      ^
      )SIC

      ⍝ H17d: larfg()'s naive square(ALPHA)/norm2_X can also UNDERflow to
      ⍝ exactly 0.0 for denormal-scale input, making BETA_r itself exactly
      ⍝ 0.0 -- which the "scale small BETA" loop could never move away
      ⍝ from (0.0 × anything is still 0.0), hanging at 100% CPU. Must
      ⍝ complete (with some deterministic result), not hang.
      ⍝
      MM←2 2⍴1J1 0 0 1E¯200J1E¯200
      ⌹MM
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹MM
      ^
      )SIC

      )ERASE MM

      ]NEXTFILE
